  '<p class="gd-p">Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.</p><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-settings-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Settings page</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with <b class="gd-ui">Open site settings</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Program settings: every timing and policy value.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Forms: Blind Spot&#39;s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:33%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:84.9%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company&#39;s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes and Quick replies.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">My profile</b>: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole (&quot;Good morning, Abbas and Mahad&quot; on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the greeting name</b>, type it and save.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-program-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Program settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking&#39;s all-in price a day) and <b class="gd-ui">Approve a renter&#39;s extension at once when nothing needs a person</b> (on). A car&#39;s own switch is in Fleet, the car, <b class="gd-ui">Edit details</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Renters extend themselves</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month&#39;s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the defaults</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Change a value and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:22%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:27.8%;top:49%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-lead-time-pricing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lead-time pricing</h2><p class="gd-p">A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: Lead-time pricing is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); <b class="gd-ui">Add a tier</b> adds one, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer</b> is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save lead-time pricing</b>. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What it touches</th><th scope="col">How</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The rental charge</td><td>The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, &quot;Short-notice pricing +10%&quot; or &quot;Booked ahead −5%&quot;. Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons</td></tr><tr><td>When it is worked out</td><td>When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. &quot;From $X a day&quot; stays at the base rate</td></tr><tr><td>When it is locked</td><td>On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage</td></tr><tr><td>Other discounts</td><td>The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it</td></tr><tr><td>Owner revenue and commissions</td><td>Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts</td></tr><tr><td>Staff</td><td>Change it on a booking under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b> on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; the car &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> &gt; Lead-time pricing for this car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-vehicle-class-rules" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle class rules</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle class rules</b>. How a new car&#39;s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a rule</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try a car</b> gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-official-serviceontario-forms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Official ServiceOntario forms</h2><p class="gd-p">The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher&#39;s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. Each form shows &quot;Mapping to check&quot; (a draft is ready) or &quot;Official PDF in use&quot;. Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Preview with</b>: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download a filled preview</b> and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or &quot;Signed here by hand, in ink&quot;), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b> lists every save, with who and when; <b class="gd-ui">Load</b> puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners &gt; Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for owners</b>. Every owner&#39;s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with <b class="gd-ui">Record an official form signed in ink</b>. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A new version from ServiceOntario? Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload the official fillable PDF</b>: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company&#39;s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner&#39;s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form&#39;s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-blind-spot-rental-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Blind Spot rental agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental&#39;s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars&#39; rental agreement and Blind Spot&#39;s own. Blind Spot&#39;s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload Blind Spot&#39;s PDF</b> and choose Blind Spot&#39;s blank form (2 pages, A4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the filled sample</b>: a made-up booking on the form. <b class="gd-ui">Sample billed to an insurer</b> also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars&#39; HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative&#39;s signature instead of Sam&#39;s.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A new version of Blind Spot&#39;s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>, and bookings keep the version in use until then.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking&#39;s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter&#39;s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the &quot;Your signed rental agreement&quot; email. Admin &gt; Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-agreements-to-sign-investors-and-staff" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements to sign: investors and staff</h2><p class="gd-p">Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person&#39;s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Investor: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b>. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Once the investor signs, the agreement shows <b class="gd-ui">Awaiting countersignature</b> on the investor&#39;s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press <b class="gd-ui">Countersign</b>. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Staff: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b>. Under Staff agreements, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b> beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field staff member&#39;s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Your own PDF instead? <b class="gd-ui">Send a PDF to sign</b> still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Sent by mistake? Press <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> and give the reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-user-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The user guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Guides</b>. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press <b class="gd-ui">Show the preview</b> to see it as people will. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the draft</b>; each save is kept in the section&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a chapter</b>. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish version</b> (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-guides-keep-up-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The guides keep up by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal&#39;s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Such a section says <b class="gd-ui">Changed automatically on</b> and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide&#39;s editor. Not right? Open the section and press <b class="gd-ui">Revert</b>: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section&#39;s history. There is nothing to review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The card &quot;The guides keep up by themselves&quot; at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-insurers-and-the-other-lists" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Insurers and the other lists</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-promo-codes-end-dates-and-reminders" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Promo codes: end dates and reminders</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Promo codes</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.</li><li>A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.</li><li>A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with &quot;This code has expired&quot;.</li><li>A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.</li><li>The list shows each code&#39;s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-card-coverage-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> is the list renters see at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer&#39;s own document, and when it was last checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer&#39;s own document unticked and the summary&#39;s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-reviews-review-requests-and-google" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reviews: review requests and Google</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile&#39;s own review link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google Business Profile: press <b class="gd-ui">Connect Google</b> and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A clear match stops that renter&#39;s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and &quot;I already left a review&quot;, Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Pair the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card reader</b>. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Generate pairing code</b>. Type the three words in <b class="gd-ui">Pairing code</b>, name the reader (Front desk) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pair reader</b>. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account&#39;s statement descriptor.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Rewards</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b>. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter&#39;s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ways to earn</b>: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend&#39;s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows &quot;Received reward points&quot;), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter&#39;s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tiers</b>: Gold from 1,000 points earned in 12 months, Platinum from 15,000, Black from 60,000 (below Gold a renter is a Member). Points earned count, so using points never lowers a tier. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> on a tier for its name and points. Tiers give perks, not discounts; tier codes issued before release 40 work until they end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Perks</b>: Instant Book (Gold), Any car, any time (Platinum) and a free rental day a year (Black). Each tier keeps the perks below it. <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a perk to move it to another tier, reword it or switch it off. <b class="gd-ui">Change the response time</b> sets how fast Fleet answers an Any car request (4 hours); the open ones are listed with their answer-by time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Points and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code, except the Black tier&#39;s free day: CarmaCars pays for it, and the owner&#39;s payout is worked out on the price before it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Google reviews claimed</b> lists every claim; <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> takes the points back with a reason. <b class="gd-ui">A renter&#39;s points</b>: find the renter, then <b class="gd-ui">Add or take off points</b> with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Setup checklist</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars&#39; own accounts. <b class="gd-ui">Add to Apple Wallet</b> stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker&#39;s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.</p><p class="gd-p">Program: <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> (on) makes every Call and Text button use the CarmaCars number in Quo (chapter Texts and calls). Off, they open the device&#39;s own phone and messages apps.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-stuck-help" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stuck? help</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Stuck? help</b>: turn it on or off, the minutes on a page without a successful action (3), and the errors (3) before the box offers the guide and the Academy lesson. <b class="gd-ui">Where people get stuck</b>, on the same page, lists the pages it showed on most in the last 30 days, with how often the guide and the lesson were opened.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">API access (Claude and scripts)</h3><p class="gd-p">Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">API access</b> connects Claude so you (or Mahad) can run CarmaCars from a Claude chat: bookings, offers, payments, refunds, returns, cars, rates, listings, owners, invoices, staff and hiring (&quot;hire Ana as customer service&quot;). <b class="gd-ui">Connect from Claude</b>: in Claude, Settings &gt; Connectors &gt; Add custom connector, paste https://carmacars.ca/api/mcp, then sign in to CarmaCars and press <b class="gd-ui">Allow</b>. Every change is two steps: Claude first shows what will change (nothing is changed yet), and does it only when you agree. Keys and connections made with every scope got the Admin scopes in release 33; a key with fewer scopes keeps them. For Claude Code or a script, <b class="gd-ui">Make a key</b>: copy it at once, it is shown only once. Each key or connection acts as its Admin, with the scopes chosen; <b class="gd-ui">Revoke</b> stops it at once. The <b class="gd-ui">Call log</b> lists every call (the previews too) with the values before and after. The database checks each action exactly as the Admin screens do.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The logo</h3><p class="gd-p">The site, every portal, every email and the documents show the brand logo. To use another, upload it under Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Site settings</b>, the Logo card (PNG or JPEG for emails and documents).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-deposits-stay-as-holds-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits stay as holds (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every deposit by card is a hold (an authorization) that stays with Stripe: it is never captured by itself, so nothing is paid out and nothing has to be refunded. Capture only what is owed, and release the rest from the booking. The booking&#39;s Security deposit panel shows Hold expires with the date Stripe gives. When a hold nears its expiry while the car is out or tickets can still come in, Finance gets a To do with <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b>: a new hold on the saved card, then the old one is released.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Extended deposit holds (up to about 30 days)</b> stays off until Stripe confirms IC+ pricing and extended authorization; when on, the hold on the saved card asks for a longer authorization and falls back to a standard one by itself. It never touches the rental payment. Capturing a deposit hold by itself is off. The heavy cleaning fee (an excessively dirty or smoked-in car) is $300 in <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>, editable as every fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-updated-terms-to-accept" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Updated terms to accept</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Updated terms</b>. When the terms of use, the privacy policy or an agreement template changes, publish the new version here; with <b class="gd-ui">Requires acceptance</b> on, each person it binds accepts it before using their portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish a version</b>. Choose the Document (the terms of use and the privacy policy bind everyone with a portal; each agreement binds the people who sign it: renters, owners, fleet suppliers, partners, investors, or staff and field).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Give the Version (for example the date it takes effect) and <b class="gd-ui">What changed</b>: people read this summary first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paste <b class="gd-ui">The new text</b>. For the terms of use or the privacy policy, leave it empty to use the site&#39;s current text; a text you paste also replaces the site&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leave <b class="gd-ui">Requires acceptance</b> on and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish a version</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Everyone it binds whose account was opened before sees <b class="gd-ui">We&#39;ve updated our terms</b> full screen on their next visit, with your summary and the text, and presses Accept. The acceptance is recorded with the time, the IP address, the device and the version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Accepted</b> on each version opens who accepted it and when.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It is a click-through acceptance of the new version: no signed agreement is voided and no renter signs the agreement of a past booking again. An Admin account is never asked.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every agreement is signed with the e-signature only (the identity steps, the IP address, the audit trail): a signature on paper is never recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form, which the government requires signed in ink, is recorded from its scan.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</h3><p class="gd-p">Program settings: <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit: percent (hundredths: 290 is 2.9%)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit: fixed part (cents)</b> (30 is $0.30). When a deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card, the renter pays this fee on it, as a separate non-refundable amount shown before they pay, on the receipt and on the Money tab. Set both to 0 to charge no fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-my-profile-and-name-changes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My profile and name changes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My profile</b> has your display name, <b class="gd-ui">Request a name change</b> for your legal name, your phone number and <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b>. When someone else asks to change the legal name on their agreements, it comes to To do with Approve and Decline, and shows on their page (owner, investor or renter). Approving changes the name on their account and record; agreements already signed keep the name they were signed with.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-ai-auto-replies-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI auto-replies (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, the AI auto-replies group, answers common questions by itself, only from the FAQ (<b class="gd-ui">Site content</b>), within Workers AI&#39;s free daily allowance. Each channel has its switch, on by default: texts to the CarmaCars number, emails to the inboxes listed (help@in.carmacars.ca), the website live chat, WhatsApp, Facebook Page messages and Instagram messages.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A question the FAQ answers gets the answer at once. A text asked between 1 am and 5 am is answered at 5 am (the quiet hours are settings).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the FAQ does not answer it, or the model is not sure enough (70%), nothing is sent: a text stays in Messages for staff, and an email or a Meta message becomes a To do for customer service, <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and the question.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each person gets at most 5 automatic answers a day, never while a staff member texted them in the last 2 hours, and none once the day&#39;s free AI allowance is used.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The card <b class="gd-ui">AI auto-replies: the last answers</b> shows today&#39;s answers and the last questions, with what was sent or why not.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Messenger, Instagram and WhatsApp need the Meta app&#39;s webhook set to https://carmacars.ca/api/webhooks/meta with the verify token shown in the settings, and the Worker secrets META_APP_SECRET (and WHATSAPP_TOKEN with the WhatsApp number id). TikTok has no inbound message path for businesses, so it is not answered.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-address-suggestions-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Address suggestions (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p">The address fields suggest Canadian addresses from the site&#39;s own address database (Statistics Canada&#39;s Open Database of Addresses, loaded by the addresses workflow, Ontario first). Google is asked only for what the database does not have, and only when its key is set.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-card-coverage-the-facts-the-booking-check-uses-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card coverage: the facts the booking check uses (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Each card also has: <b class="gd-ui">Network</b> (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), <b class="gd-ui">Includes rental car damage coverage (CDW)</b> (Yes, No or Unknown), <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle types not covered</b> (comma separated: exotic, luxury, truck, van, off_road, antique, motorcycle, limousine, rv), <b class="gd-ui">Must decline the rental company&#39;s CDW</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Must pay the full rental on the card</b>. A renter on card coverage picks their card from this list; the site checks it against the car&#39;s value (the Black Book value or the estimate on the car), the car&#39;s type and the length of the rental, and refuses a card that does not cover it. Unknown sends the renter to staff review. Exotic makes are listed in <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Coverage checks</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-fuel-prices-and-delivery-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fuel prices and delivery (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Program</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Fuel and charging at the return</b>: the local pump prices of regular, premium and diesel (a litre), the multiplier (1.25), the refuelling fee ($20), the price a kWh for electric cars ($0.40), and the tank and battery sizes for a car without its own. Update the pump prices every week: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> reminds you after 7 days.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Airports and delivery</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Delivery rate and origin</b>: the base fee each way ($75), the km it includes from the company&#39;s location (15), the rate per km after them ($2), and the straight line to road distance factor (1.3) used when the maps service gives no road distance. A car whose rate card has its own delivery or pickup fee keeps it; every other car follows the base.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-automatic-answers-and-email-budgets-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Automatic answers and email budgets (release 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Automatic answers: each channel (text, email, chat, social messages) switches on or off, with the quiet hours, the daily limit per person and how sure the answer must be. The last answers and the questions left for a person show in settings and under renter messages; a question it cannot answer becomes a To do. They stay inside the free daily AI allowance.</li><li>Email budgets: Settings, Usage shows the real daily email capacity of all our sending services together (Cloudflare included), and when a service is not sending, why. Receipts, signed copies and staff messages always go.</li><li>First photo: each listing chooses its first photo, the plain car, a car-show photo with a model, or a flyer with the live price; the flyer is made again when the price changes.</li><li>Rewards: points for a photo with a review and for every rental after the first; every way to earn is on the renter&#39;s Rewards page.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-owner-emails-trips-and-the-week-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner emails: trips and the week (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">Owners are not emailed when a booking comes in, is confirmed or changes, because many bookings are cancelled (owner_new_booking, owner_booking_confirmed and owner_booking_changed are off, with their texts and notices). They are emailed when a trip is complete and the car is back (owner_trip_completed: the car, dates, days, distance driven if recorded and their share, which says it shows on the next statement while the booking&#39;s revenue is hidden from them), and every Monday at about 9:00 Toronto time (owner_weekly_summary: per car, last week&#39;s trips with their share, the confirmed bookings of the next 14 days with dates only, and the month so far, provisional), only when there was activity. Only bookings that count toward the owner&#39;s revenue are used, never Owner Bookings or Turo trips. The Monday email has a switch in Program settings: <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary email to owners</b> (on by default).</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 2621 END
